.\" robodr-agentd(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-agentd/src/bin/robodr-agentd.rs and the configuration
.\" reference in crates/robodr-agentd/README.md. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-AGENTD 8 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-agentd \- RoboDR live daemon: ROS 2 discovery and events \(-> decision chain \(-> signed black box \(-> OCSF findings spool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-agentd
.B \-\-config
.I agentd.json
.RB [ \-\-check\-config ]
.PP
.B robodr\-agentd
.RB ( \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B robodr\-agentd
reads RTPS discovery traffic (live AF_PACKET capture or a pcap replay) and
RobotEvent JSON Lines (standard input or a unix socket), runs them through
the ROS 2 pipeline and the RoboDR decision chain, records evidence in a signed
black box and writes validated OCSF findings to a spool directory. It reports
its own health and is never "OK" while blind.
.PP
It is read\-only on networks and protective only: response plans are
recorded, never executed. It does not override the platform's safety system,
e\-stop or command authority.
.PP
Normally started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.IR robodr\-agentd.service ,
with
.I /etc/robodr/agentd.json
and the black\-box key handed over as a systemd credential.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
The daemon configuration (JSON). Parsing is strict: unknown keys are refused at
every level, and every path must be absolute. See
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/agentd.example.json
and the crate README for the sections
.RI ( robot ", " sensor ", " policy_path ", " blackbox ", " spool ", "
.IR event_inputs ", " context ", " firewall ", " motion_monitor ", " daemon ).
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the configuration and load every file it names (profile, policy,
monitor config, key file), print warnings, then exit without starting.
The profile trust and anti\-rollback decision is made, but the state file is
not written (only a starting daemon records an accepted version).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.SH KEY
Keys are never accepted on the command line.
.B blackbox.key_file
is either a
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)
secret key file as written by
.B robodr\-blackbox keygen
(Ed25519 by default, or a legacy HMAC\-SHA256 key file; its key id is used,
and a
.B blackbox.key_id
that contradicts it is a configuration error) or a bare hex HMAC key of at
least 32 bytes (0.1.0\-alpha.1 format). The file is refused if it is a
symlink or not a regular file, if group or others have any access to it, if
it is owned by a uid other than the daemon's or root, if it is larger than
4 KiB, or if it is a public key file
.RI ( .pub ).
With Ed25519 the evidence is verified with the public key file alone
.RB ( "robodr\-blackbox verify \-\-keyring" " \fIFILE\fR.pub)"
and verifiers cannot forge it. HMAC keys load with a start\-up warning: the
verifying side holds the same secret and could forge evidence.
.SH PROFILE TRUST
.B sensor.profile_trust
decides whether a locked profile is enforced:
.B trusted_keys
(a
.I robodr\-profile\-trust/v1
file of Ed25519 public keys; without it no locked profile is enforced),
.B state_file
(anti\-rollback: a lower
.BR profile_version ,
the same version with different bytes, or a draft replacing a locked profile
is refused),
.B allow_rollback
(the exact
.B sha256:
digest of the one older file to accept; remove it afterwards),
.B expect_platform
and
.BR expect_unit_id .
The profile must be accompanied by its detached signature
.IB profile_path .sig
as written by
.BR "robodr\-commission lock \-\-sign\-key" .
A profile that fails any check runs observe\-only and is reported as
.BR robot.ros2.profile_refused .
The profile version in findings is the signed
.BR metadata.profile_version ;
.B robot.profile_version
was removed and is refused with a message saying so.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
and
.B SIGINT
stop the daemon cleanly: the black box is sealed and its checkpoint is copied
to the spool.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean stop (signal, or every input ended with
.BR daemon.exit_when_inputs_end ).
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (for example the black box could not be sealed).
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8;
nothing was started. The systemd unit does not restart on this status.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/agentd.json
Configuration (operator\-created, 0640 root:robodr).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/agentd\-blackbox.key
Black\-box key (0600 root:root); the unit exposes a copy at
.IR /run/credentials/robodr\-agentd.service/blackbox.key .
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/blackbox/agentd/
Black\-box segments and checkpoint (single writer).
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/spool/agentd/
OCSF findings spool.
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/profile.json\fR, \fI/etc/robodr/profile.json.sig
Locked profile and its detached signature (0640 root:robodr).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/profile\-trust.json
Trusted profile signing keys (public; 0644 root:root, never group/other
writable).
.TP
.I /var/lib/robodr/profile\-state/agentd.json
Anti\-rollback state (suggested path; the directory must be writable by the
daemon).
.TP
.I /run/robodr\-agentd/
Runtime directory for an optional unix\-socket event input (socket mode 0600).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-pack (1),
.BR robodr\-pulsard (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
